course: dictionary
lesson: 16175
title: What www means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You will often see www at the start of a website address. It is a short way of writing a longer name: World Wide Web. The web is the collection of pages you can visit on the internet using a web browser.
explain: «Mum typed www dot library dot example into the browser and the homepage opened.» Here www sits at the start of the web address, and the browser uses it to find the pages on that site.
explain: The internet and the web are not the same thing. The internet is the network of connected computers. The web is the pages you read on it. If you find a website you do not know, ask an adult before you visit it.
fact: www stands for World Wide Web.
fact: The web is the pages and sites you visit on the internet.
fact: The internet is the network of connected computers, and the web is the pages on it.
fact: You use a web browser to open and read pages on the web.
fact: www often appears at the start of a web address, such as «www dot» followed by the name of the site.
exercise: What does www stand for? | Wild Web Worlds | Wide World Web | *World Wide Web | Web World Wide
exercise: «Type the web address, www dot library dot example, into the browser.» Where does www usually appear in a web address? | Only in emails | In the middle of every word | *At the start
exercise: Which sentence explains the difference between the internet and the web? | The internet is the pages; the web is the computers | They mean exactly the same thing | *The internet is the network of connected computers; the web is the pages on it | The web is a kind of computer game
test: A child finds a new website and wants to visit it. What should they do first? | *Ask an adult before visiting | Click every link quickly | Share their password with the site | Turn off the computer for ever
test: What does a web browser help you do? | *Open and read pages on the web | Print a photo on paper | Cook dinner | Count the numbers in a sum
exam: Which of these is most like a web address? | 12 plus 7 | Two bags of crisps | *www dot animals dot example | A red bicycle
